Issues.Body:
### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

compiler-cli

### Is this a regression?

Yes

### Description

`[attr.onerror]` in a template is rejected with `NG5002`. `@HostBinding('attr.onerror')` is not validated, and neither is the same host metadata in a library's partial declaration. Both build clean in dev and production, and the bound value becomes an inline handler.

### directive in the app

```ts
@Directive({ selector: 'img[imageFallback]' })
export class ImageFallback {
  @Input() imageFallback = '';

  @HostBinding('attr.onerror')
  get fallback() {
    return `this.src='${this.imageFallback}'`;
  }
}
```

```html
<img src="/missing.png" [imageFallback]="product.fallback" />
```

`product.fallback` is a product field from an API. A quote in it closes the
string literal.

**Case 2, same directive from a library** in partial (linker) format:

```js
host: { properties: { 'attr.onerror': 'this.fallback' } }
```

The app only binds the input, and `ng-packagr` reports nothing when publishing, so there is no diagnostic on either side of the dependency boundary.

The guard is `BindingParser.createBoundHostProperties`, reachedonly through `verifyHostBindings`. That has one call site, `extractHostBindings` in [jit_compiler_facade.ts:949](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/22.2.3/packages/compiler/src/jit_compiler_facade.ts#L949), so it runs under JIT only. ngtsc merges `@HostBinding` decorators in [typecheck/host_bindings.ts (https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/22.2.3/packages/compiler/src/typecheck/host_bindings.ts#L116) and the linker reads host metadata straight from the partial declaration; neither calls it.

Both paths emit `ɵɵattribute("onerror", ctx.fallback)` with two arguments, so no sanitizer runs: event attributes have no security context. Nothing re-checks at runtime either. `validateAgainstEventProperties` is for properties and runs under `ngDevMode && firstUpdatePass`, and `ɵɵvalidateAttribute` is registered only for `iframe@sandbox` and the SVG `animate` family.

### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug

See https://github.com/SkyZeroZx/attr-validation-bypass
